{:edb/db-before-t 378 :edb/db-after-t 379 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533691 50 #inst "2026-10-04T17:10:50.011Z" 13194139533691 true] [17592186096723 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247192 13194139533691 true] [17592186096723 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247213 13194139533691 true] [17592186096723 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247216 13194139533691 true] [17592186096723 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247220 13194139533691 true] [17592186096723 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247250 13194139533691 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247157 13194139533691 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247164 13194139533691 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247171 13194139533691 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247178 13194139533691 true] [17592186096724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247223 13194139533691 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247185 13194139533691 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247206 13194139533691 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247226 13194139533691 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247229 13194139533691 true] [17592186096725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247257 13194139533691 true] [17592186096726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247199 13194139533691 true] [17592186096726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247233 13194139533691 true] [17592186096726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247236 13194139533691 true] [17592186096726 1020 #edb/ref 17592186247243 13194139533691 true] [17592186097181 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533691 true] [17592186097181 1145 "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})\\cdot g(\\frac{7}{2})-f(\\frac{7}{2})\\cdot {g}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})}{{(g(\\frac{7}{2}))}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFrom the graph above, we obtain that $f(\\frac{7}{2})=g(\\frac{7}{2})=1.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (3,4)$ equals $-2.$ So, ${f}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})=-2.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (2,4)$ equals $0.$ So, ${g}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})=0.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})g(\\frac{7}{2})-f(\\frac{7}{2}){g}^{′}(\\frac{7}{2})}{{(g(\\frac{7}{2}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (1)-1\\cdot 0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247158 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1089 "q-104785" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/df4fed951351dfc1203ba6257f404a5efadbec37b9f11098af1fc36a7793b0c7.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find ${h}^{′}(2)$ where $h(x)=g(x)-f(x).$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1113 #uuid "a5313490-e072-582c-a40a-04691b38c4c3" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1138 false 13194139533691 true] [17592186247157 1145 "The addition and constant multiple rules for derivatives give\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x)-{f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(2)={g}^{′}(2)-{f}^{′}(2).\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that $x=2$ corresponds to\n\n- the interval $x\\in (-1,3)$ for the function $f,$ and\n\n- the interval $x\\in (-1,3)$ for the function $g,$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/814ce0fdce1428b3bd619caa5e8d09a828d2f2c52fd0b20b7f520562319fb848.png)\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-1,3)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{4-1}{3-(-1)}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-1,3)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δg}{Δx}=\\frac{1-4}{3-(-1)}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${g}^{′}(2)=-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & ={g}^{′}(2)-{f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247159 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247160 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247161 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247162 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247163 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1041 "selection" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247160 13194139533691 true] [17592186247158 1110 #uuid "a7858f1b-2dfb-5eeb-8306-77b5aedb44e5" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247159 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247159 1111 #uuid "609f09b0-d1f8-58f2-99e9-5e5ffd85b202" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247160 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247160 1111 #uuid "bfe29d5d-1885-5216-ac5e-ef4d283127b9" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247161 1034 "1" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247161 1111 #uuid "0d3cd0a8-5856-5442-8079-314f07989acf" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247162 1034 "0" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247162 1111 #uuid "88cb7e1b-20d8-52bb-9e5d-5d41a442ce54" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247163 1034 "-1" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247163 1111 #uuid "42b3bc5c-eced-58de-a806-7405047313e6" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247165 13194139533691 true] [17592186247164 1089 "q-104786" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533691 true] [17592186247164 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/7c4260d8cdf3557b6c6f762bf83862297812368d5211