)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find ${h}^{′}(-2)$ where $h(x)=f(x)g(x).$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247185 1113 #uuid "fb55d485-2644-5851-8653-521b712ca5e8" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247185 1138 false 13194139533691 true] [17592186247185 1145 "The product rule and the addition rule for derivatives give\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(-2)={f}^{′}(-2)\\cdot g(-2)+f(-2)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-2).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-2)=0$ and $g(-2)=3.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,0)$ equals $-1.$ So, ${f}^{′}(-2)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,0)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${g}^{′}(-2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-2) & ={f}^{′}(-2)\\cdot g(-2)+f(-2)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-2)-{f}^{′}(-2) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247187 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247188 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247189 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247190 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247191 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1041 "selection" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247189 13194139533691 true] [17592186247186 1110 #uuid "9a615ce6-7471-5030-95ec-c1833fea511c" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247187 1034 "-\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247187 1111 #uuid "7c479a53-aba3-514b-8d2a-b393006acc6b" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247188 1034 "2" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247188 1111 #uuid "1d910462-bf9a-52f9-b9e2-d05f3e92f579" 13194139533691 true]