 1145 "To compute ${f}^{′}(-1.5),$ we need to find the slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ at $x=-1.5.$\n\nLet's consider the graph of $y=f(x)$ on $[-2,1].$ Notice that $x=-1.5$ lies in this interval.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/2216d3014a8c74102d5e298c300092a575798de0b66d89914716898bc16ac655.png)\n\nThe slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in (-2,1)$ is constant and equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{0-2}{1-(-2)}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(-1.5)=-\\frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247252 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247253 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247254 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247255 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247256 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1041 "selection" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247252 13194139533691 true] [17592186247251 1110 #uuid "10520adf-d332-589c-ae04-87c6c7b12fe1" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247252 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247252 1111 #uuid "c2a24471-b797-5f26-9414-4bc786408249" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247253 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247253 1111 #uuid "45dd0e8e-084a-5f7e-a202-6f4caa37c4d3" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247254 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247254 1111 #uuid "7f47ba29-e2bf-5601-890b-6a7afc994def" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247255 1034 "-1" 13194139533691 true] [17592186247255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533691 true] [17592186247255 1111 #uuid "42a2c461-914a-59a7-896f-f2bf322d